  "notes": "USAGE:\nA formal verb used primarily in media and journalism contexts. The alternative form {報|ほう}ずる also exists but is less common in modern Japanese. Often seen in passive form: 〜と{報|ほう}じられている (it is reported that ~).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {事件|じけん}を{報|ほう}じる (to report an incident)\n- 〜と{報|ほう}じられている (it is reported that ~)\n- {大|おお}きく{報|ほう}じる (to cover extensively)\n- {一斉|いっせい}に{報|ほう}じる (to report simultaneously)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {報道|ほうどう}する: to report (news) — more common as a する-verb\n- {伝|つた}える: to convey, to report — broader usage, not limited to media",
